From: fexdroid
Subject: [PATCH] JIT: load call return addresses from a literal pool

A call pushes its return address to the guest stack and to the call-ret
stack. The address is a guest RIP, built with movz+movk+movk for a 64-bit
guest above 4GB (Dota 2 code sits at 0x73xxxxxxxx), and with four
instructions whenever relocatable constants are on (DiskCache writing, code
cache validation), because relocated moves are padded.

The return address is only stored, so a load is as good as a move chain
there. It now comes from a new IR op, EntrypointOffsetLiteral, which the
backend emits as one `ldr xN, <literal>` (`ldr wN` for a 32-bit guest,
which loads the low half). The literals are placed in a pool after the jump
thunks of the multiblock, out of the straight-line code, 8-byte aligned.
Each slot carries a RELOC_GUEST_RIP_LITERAL relocation, the type the jump
thunks and the block tail already use for their GuestRIP fields, so
DiskCache stores it relative to the block entry and fixes it up when cached
code is loaded at another guest base. The load is PC-relative and moves
with the code when the temporary buffer is copied, so it needs no fixup.

Moves stay where they are as short: a guest RIP below 4GB without
relocation padding (at most two moves). They also stay when the multiblock
was restarted with far jumps; a load out of the +-1MB range restarts the
compilation that way, through the existing bind-or-restart path.

Every other EntrypointOffset (RIP-relative data bases, compares, atomics)
keeps the move chain: there the value feeds an address or a compare, and a
load from a code line, likely missing in L1D, would be on the critical path.

Local patch, not upstream.
---
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp
index 3691bca..3535597 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/ALUOps.cpp
@@ -64,6 +64,19 @@ DEF_OP(EntrypointOffset) {
   InsertGuestRIPMove(GetReg(Node), Constant & Mask);
 }
 
+DEF_OP(EntrypointOffsetLiteral) {
+  auto Op = IROp->C<IR::IROp_EntrypointOffsetLiteral>();
+
+  auto Constant = Entry + Op->Offset;
+  uint64_t Mask = ~0ULL;
+  const auto OpSize = IROp->Size;
+  if (OpSize == IR::OpSize::i32Bit) {
+    Mask = 0xFFFF'FFFFULL;
+  }
+
+  InsertGuestRIPLiteralLoad(GetReg(Node), Constant & Mask, OpSize);
+}
+
 DEF_OP(PatchableGuestData) {
   auto Op = IROp->C<IR::IROp_PatchableGuestData>();
   InsertGuestPatchableDataMove(GetReg(Node), Op->Value, Op->SiteAddress, (uint8_t)Op->SiteSize);
diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/Arm64Relocations.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/Arm64Relocations.cpp
index 5877844..b55811f 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/Arm64Relocations.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/Arm64Relocations.cpp
@@ -103,6 +103,47 @@ void Arm64JITCore::InsertGuestRIPMove(ARMEmitter::Register Reg, uint64_t Constan
   Relocations.emplace_back(MoveABI);
 }
 
+void Arm64JITCore::InsertGuestRIPLiteralLoad(ARMEmitter::Register Reg, uint64_t Constant, IR::OpSize Size) {
+  const bool Is32Bit = Size == IR::OpSize::i32Bit;
+
+  // Without relocation padding, a guest RIP below 4GB takes at most two moves. One load isn't worth its
+  // latency and the data cache line it touches there. Higher addresses take three moves, and with
+  // relocation padding every guest RIP takes four.
+  const bool ShortMove = !SupportCodeRelocations && (Is32Bit || (Constant >> 32) == 0);
+
+  // The literal pool sits after the jump thunks, out of reach of a literal load (+-1MB) only in a
+  // multiblock large enough to need far branches. Use moves there.
+  if (ShortMove || RequiresFarARM64Jumps) {
+    InsertGuestRIPMove(Reg, Constant);
+    return;
+  }
+
+  auto& Lit = PendingGuestRIPLiterals.emplace_back(PendingGuestRIPLiteral {.GuestRIP = Constant, .Label = {}});
+  if (Is32Bit) {
+    // Loads the lower half of the 64-bit literal, which is also correct after relocation.
+    ldr(Reg.W(), &Lit.Label);
+  } else {
+    ldr(Reg.X(), &Lit.Label);
+  }
+}
+
+void Arm64JITCore::PlaceGuestRIPLiterals() {
+  if (PendingGuestRIPLiterals.empty()) {
+    return;
+  }
+
+  // Natural alignment for the 64-bit loads. The code is copied to a 16B aligned location, and DiskCache loads it to one.
+  Align(8);
+  for (auto& Pending : PendingGuestRIPLiterals) {
+    auto Lit = InsertGuestRIPLiteral(Pending.GuestRIP);
+    Lit.Loc = std::move(Pending.Label);
+    // Binds the label, emits the literal and records a RELOC_GUEST_RIP_LITERAL at its offset.
+    // Restarts the compilation with far jumps when a load is out of range.
+    PlaceNamedSymbolLiteral(std::move(Lit));
+  }
+  PendingGuestRIPLiterals.clear();
+}
+
 auto Arm64JITCore::InsertGuestPatchableRIPLiteral(uint64_t GuestRIP, uint64_t SiteAddress, uint8_t ValueSize) -> NamedSymbolLiteralPair {
   return {
     .Lit = GuestRIP,
